Q: How to obtain full body in Axum handler? A: <p>Here is a concrete example using <a href="https://docs.rs/axum/latest/axum/trait.RequestExt.html#tymethod.extract" rel="nofollow noreferrer">RequestExt::extract</a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>use axum::{RequestExt, response::IntoResponse, extract::Request, body::Bytes};

async fn handler(request: Request) -&gt; impl IntoResponse {
    let body = request.extract::&lt;Bytes, _&gt;().await.unwrap();

    // preform the transformation on body

    let body = axum::body::Body::from(body);
    Response::builder().status(200).body(body).unwrap()
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to display two-line Suggestion menu with NSTextField A: <p>The hack is to use initialiser with <code>AttributedString</code>  <strong><code>public</code></strong><code> </code><strong><code>init</code></strong><code>(representedValue: SuggestionItemType, attributedTitle: AttributedString)</code> and &quot;force&quot; font using <code>setAttributes</code></p>
<p>Another important note: If your minimum deployment target is macOS10.13 with <strong><code>@available</code></strong><code>(macOS 15, *)</code> macro -&gt; you will still get some layout glitches. The glitches disappear with macOS10.15 as a minimum target.</p>
<pre><code>    func locationItem(_ searchCompletion: MKLocalSearchCompletion) -&gt; Item {

        var attributedTitle = AttributedString(searchCompletion.title)
        attributedTitle.setAttributes(
            AttributeContainer([
                .font: NSFont.systemFont(ofSize: NSFont.systemFontSize)
            ])
        )
        var item = NSSuggestionItem(representedValue: searchCompletion, attributedTitle: attributedTitle)

        if !searchCompletion.subtitle.isEmpty {
            item.secondaryTitle = searchCompletion.subtitle
        }

        return item
    }
</code></pre>
